{"data": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113380233017491456"]}, "author_id": "2110354767163629570", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:21:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113380267142324416"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/vo5C32MaWi", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TwilightSignals/status/2113380267142324416/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113380233017491456", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/vo5C32MaWi"}, {"display_url": "x.com/Nature/status/…", "end": 325, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Nature/status/2113355702345363659", "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/GZKkobon1S"}]}, "id": "2113380267142324416", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113355702345363659", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Prime editing works inside a human body for the first time\n\nA high-precision gene-editing method, prime editing, has rewritten DNA directly inside a patient for the first time. In a Prime Medicine trial for Wilson disease, it fixed a mutation in liver cells that stops the body https://t.co/vo5C32MaWi https://t.co/GZKkobon1S", "url": "https://x.com/TwilightSignals/status/2113380267142324416"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113309782740180992"]}, "author_id": "2110437865809174528", "created_at": "2026-10-22T16:41:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113309874721636356"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 168, "start": 155, "tag": "PrimeEditing"}, {"end": 181, "start": 169, "tag": "RareDisease"}], "urls": [{"description": "Can rewriting DNA change the future for families living with rare g...", "display_url": "youtu.be/bsjvU2BFTxo", "end": 235, "expanded_url": "https://youtu.be/bsjvU2BFTxo", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113671241869529089/oR_KlCwc?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113671241869529089/oR_KlCwc?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 212, "status": 200, "title": "David Liu: Gene Editing to Treat Rare Disease", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bsjvU2BFTxo&feature=youtu.be", "url": "https://t.co/r1ZeMwYDyo"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/5GEaYBQR3p", "end": 259, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/GENErationHopee/status/2113309874721636356/video/1", "media_key": "13_2113309782740180992", "start": 236, "url": "https://t.co/5GEaYBQR3p"}]}, "id": "2113309874721636356", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Two missing DNA letters left this patient without a working immune system and on ten pills a day. Prime editing put them back. Dr. David R. Liu explains.\n\n#PrimeEditing #RareDisease\n\nWatch the full conversation: https://t.co/r1ZeMwYDyo https://t.co/5GEaYBQR3p", "url": "https://x.com/GENErationHopee/status/2113309874721636356"}, {"author_id": "712911249281974273", "created_at": "2026-10-22T16:33:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113307651472056567"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 23, "start": 18, "tag": "BEAM"}]}, "id": "2113307651472056567", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 72, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Beam Therapeutics $BEAM  is a Blue Ocean holding in the Money Market Portfolio that is developing base-editing technology to change a single DNA base without cutting both strands, an approach still in early clinical testing. The shares have sat near $24 since mid-September, under", "url": "https://x.com/Bicepmonkey/status/2113307651472056567"}, {"author_id": "1580408538119417856", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:29:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113382134920683539"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - Application of the high-precision technique is part of a clinical trial to treat a genetic disease that can cause liver and nerve damage.", "display_url": "nature.com/articles/d4158…", "end": 153, "expanded_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03371-x", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113359869277593601/9vi5mD1x?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1066}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113359869277593601/9vi5mD1x?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 130, "status": 200, "title": "A first for CRISPR: powerful prime editing alters DNA directly in the human body", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03371-x?error=cookies_not_supported&code=943859e7-67e1-482b-be5d-3371b22dab20", "url": "https://t.co/uh9p0dENHE"}]}, "id": "2113382134920683539", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 183, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "高精度ゲノム編集法「prime editing」をヒト体内で直接用いる初の治療が臨床試験で実施され、肝障害や神経障害を引き起こす遺伝性疾患を対象に、DNAを切断せず狙った配列を書き換える治療の実用化に向けた進展を紹介した記事がNature誌に掲載されました。\nhttps://t.co/uh9p0dENHE", "url": "https://x.com/iPatho1/status/2113382134920683539"}, {"author_id": "2005886288998887424", "created_at": "2026-10-22T13:26:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113260589179183562"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "PRME"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/BreakoutBiotec…", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/BreakoutBiotech/status/2111918170667950392", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/q9aLl3PzZC"}]}, "id": "2113260589179183562", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 1449, "like_count": 26, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2111918170667950392", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "$PRME One of the aspects I like most about Prime's platform is the modularity and how it positions them to capitalize on recent FDA efforts to streamline approvals and make bespoke genetic medicine more scalable.\n\nAlthough prime editing can theoretically repair most genetic https://t.co/q9aLl3PzZC", "url": "https://x.com/BreakoutBiotech/status/2113260589179183562"}, {"author_id": "2321130066", "created_at": "2026-10-22T18:51:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113342391570534618"], "id": "2113342391570534618", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 43, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Examination of DNA Typewriter Technology: Implications for Human Biological Lineage Tracing and Developmental Coherence \nAuthor: Grok (xAI) – Executing User Directive on Human Bio Examination \nDate: October 22, 2026 \nVersion: 1.4 – Focused Biological Examination \nReference: Allen", "url": "https://x.com/Tlockty/status/2113342391570534618"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112085470175961088"]}, "author_id": "348971658", "created_at": "2026-10-22T06:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113148348387688573"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 153, "start": 146, "tag": "CRISPR"}, {"end": 166, "start": 154, "tag": "GeneTherapy"}, {"end": 182, "start": 167, "tag": "Bioinformatics"}], "urls": [{"description": "CRO specializing in drug discovery, NGS analysis, molecular simulations, and bioinformatics training. Serving global researchers since 2009.", "display_url": "bdglifesciences.com/event/crispr-g…", "end": 144, "expanded_url": "https://bdglifesciences.com/event/crispr-gene-therapy-online-workshop", "images": [{"height": 794, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112163147960254464/vCdStwKV?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112163147960254464/vCdStwKV?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 121, "status": 200, "title": "BDG LifeSciences | Bioinformatics CRO & Life Sciences Training", "unwound_url": "https://bdglifesciences.com/event/crispr-gene-therapy-online-workshop", "url": "https://t.co/M0zFp5P6Xt"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/7TBcJYUYKY", "end": 206, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/biodiscovery/status/2113148348387688573/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2112085470175961088", "start": 183, "url": "https://t.co/7TBcJYUYKY"}]}, "id": "2113148348387688573", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Day 1 of 10. Starting tonight, 9:00 PM IST.\n\nLive CRISPR &amp; gene therapy workshop, from PAM basics to HDR templates.\n\nhttps://t.co/M0zFp5P6Xt\n\n#CRISPR #GeneTherapy #Bioinformatics https://t.co/7TBcJYUYKY", "url": "https://x.com/biodiscovery/status/2113148348387688573"}, {"author_id": "244870035", "created_at": "2026-10-22T11:02:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113224533859533296"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 226, "start": 218, "tag": "Gattaca"}, {"end": 234, "start": 227, "tag": "CRISPR"}], "urls": [{"description": "Genetic manipulation has been one of the most rapidly developing branches of biotechnology over the last 20 years. With the advent of the CRISPR technique, the possibility of correcting, changing and deleting genes in a DNA sequence has become a scientific possibility. Film plots are often a realistic reflection of psychosocial aspects of the population, which can be used in educational settings to show the consequences of certain situations or moral dilemmas. From a didactic point of view, this study interprets the most significant sequences of the film Gattaca (1997), by Andrew Niccol, where, in a futuristic environment, a distinction is made between inferior human beings who have not been genetically treated and have low status functions, or superior human beings who have been genetically treated and are mainly destined for more important functions such as space travel. The main objective is to facilitate the understanding of concepts related to genetic manipulation, such as genetic", "display_url": "doi.org/10.14201/RMC.3…", "end": 259, "expanded_url": "https://doi.org/10.14201/RMC.30822", "start": 236, "status": 200, "title": "El cine en el aprendizaje de la manipulación genética a través de ciencia ficción en Gattaca (1997)", "unwound_url": "https://revistas.usal.es/cinco/index.php/medicina_y_cine/article/view/30822", "url": "https://t.co/Gu9gtRQiz6"}]}, "id": "2113224533859533296", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Gattaca se estrenó en 1997, doce años antes de que existiera CRISPR.\n\nY sigue siendo la mejor herramienta que conozco para discutir edición genética con estudiantes.\n\nLa ciencia ficción no predice: prepara el debate.\n\n#Gattaca #CRISPR\n\nhttps://t.co/Gu9gtRQiz6", "url": "https://x.com/javieralmelabae/status/2113224533859533296"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["7_2113261597363724289"]}, "author_id": "4896666378", "created_at": "2026-10-22T13:30:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113261617399886172"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 263, "start": 256, "tag": "CRISPR"}, {"end": 273, "start": 264, "tag": "Genomics"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/s1BWADNN2j", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/cbirtofficial/status/2113261617399886172/video/1", "media_key": "7_2113261597363724289", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/s1BWADNN2j"}]}, "id": "2113261617399886172", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 70, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Bacteria have a memory for viruses. 🦠 They store snippets of viral DNA in their CRISPR region to recognise the same virus next time, the system that later inspired CRISPR gene editing.\n\nSource: Barrangou et al., Science (2007) doi:10.1126/science.1138140\n\n#CRISPR #Genomics https://t.co/s1BWADNN2j", "url": "https://x.com/cbirtofficial/status/2113261617399886172"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113231620043853824"]}, "author_id": "158774224", "created_at": "2026-10-22T11:30:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113231630269624517"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/vr8SplLU9m", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ChileBio_AG/status/2113231630269624517/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113231620043853824", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.co/vr8SplLU9m"}]}, "id": "2113231630269624517", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 56, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "¿Aceite de soya superando al de oliva en grasas saludables? 🫒🌱\n\nCientíficos en Corea del Sur usaron CRISPR para llevar el ácido oleico en soya hasta un récord de 90,2% (vs 20% habitual) y recortar más de 40% las grasas saturadas 🧬🫀\n\nDetalles de la investigación aquí 👇\n🔗 https://t.co/vr8SplLU9m", "url": "https://x.com/ChileBio_AG/status/2113231630269624517"}, {"author_id": "1687416489308008449", "created_at": "2026-10-22T05:09:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113135740469010866"], "id": "2113135740469010866", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 244, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "CRISPR is no longer science fiction. 🧬\n\nIn July 2026, the FDA expanded approval of CRISPR therapy Casgevy to children as young as 2 with sickle cell disease or beta-thalassemia [1].\n\nIn 2025, researchers reported the first personalized CRISPR treatment for a baby with a rare", "url": "https://x.com/sciqst/status/2113135740469010866"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113363761549492225"]}, "author_id": "480582261", "created_at": "2026-10-22T20:16:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113363764107936233"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 49, "start": 42, "tag": "ASHG26"}, {"end": 152, "start": 146, "tag": "8146T"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/sIxTfjFO2f", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/nabsys/status/2113363764107936233/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113363761549492225", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/sIxTfjFO2f"}]}, "id": "2113363764107936233", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 56, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Nabsys is presenting two posters today at #ASHG26, exploring new applications of Electronic Genome Mapping (EGM) in genomic research. 🧬\n\n🔬 Poster #8146T: Genome-Scale Mapping of Human LINE-1 ORF2p Endonuclease Activity presented by Michael Gallagher, PhD, Software Applications https://t.co/sIxTfjFO2f", "url": "https://x.com/nabsys/status/2113363764107936233"}, {"author_id": "818008252814217217", "created_at": "2026-10-21T21:52:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113025540965957721"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 222, "start": 215, "tag": "CRISPR"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "doi.org/10.1016/j.canl…", "end": 188, "expanded_url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.canlet.2026.218887", "start": 165, "unwound_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0304383526006518", "url": "https://t.co/kYmLhcmyGG"}]}, "id": "2113025540965957721", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 204, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "“Genome-wide CRISPR screen identifies PKMYT1 inhibition as a synthetic lethal vulnerability in IDH1-mutant glioma”\nLang F [..] Yang C.\nCancer Lett 2026-10-08/11-28.\nhttps://t.co/kYmLhcmyGG\n\n… Through a whole-genome #CRISPR screen", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceCrisp/status/2113025540965957721"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113357252862091264"]}, "author_id": "1682144833953996801", "created_at": "2026-10-22T19:50:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113357258281116142"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 145, "start": 140, "tag": "EGFR"}, {"end": 154, "start": 146, "tag": "domains"}, {"end": 163, "start": 155, "tag": "biotech"}, {"end": 173, "start": 164, "tag": "oncology"}, {"end": 192, "start": 174, "tag": "SuperIntelligence"}, {"end": 199, "start": 193, "tag": "DotSI"}, {"end": 207, "start": 200, "tag": "CRISPR"}, {"end": 211, "start": 208, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 221, "start": 212, "tag": "genomics"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "EGFR.si", "end": 23, "expanded_url": "https://EGFR.si", "start": 0, "unwound_url": "https://EGFR.si", "url": "https://t.co/9FlcHC6Fov"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Zh8AFpkcCU", "end": 245, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/names_plug/status/2113357258281116142/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113357252862091264", "start": 222, "url": "https://t.co/Zh8AFpkcCU"}]}, "id": "2113357258281116142", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/9FlcHC6Fov — 4L gene domain — generic, \n\nEGFR Super Intelligence — AI drug discovery — oncology — CRISPR — precision medicine\n\n#EGFR #domains #biotech #oncology #SuperIntelligence #DotSI #CRISPR #AI #genomics https://t.co/Zh8AFpkcCU", "url": "https://x.com/DomaintronSi/status/2113357258281116142"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113367084801331201"]}, "author_id": "1846633730317692928", "created_at": "2026-10-22T20:29:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113367103374033207"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "sciencedirect.com/science/articl…", "end": 23, "expanded_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1931312826004063", "start": 0, "unwound_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/user/error/ATN-20?errorContext=arp-beb82387-4361-4d96-956d-4a43c90bcf59", "url": "https://t.co/mdj6Sdj32r"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/n6oG3Gdtci", "end": 123, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Thoandas/status/2113367103374033207/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113367084801331201", "start": 100, "url": "https://t.co/n6oG3Gdtci"}]}, "id": "2113367103374033207", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/mdj6Sdj32r\nA phage-encoded small RNA that mimics chimeric guide to inhibit CRISPR-Cas9 https://t.co/n6oG3Gdtci", "url": "https://x.com/Thoandas/status/2113367103374033207"}, {"author_id": "21558596", "created_at": "2026-10-22T08:36:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113187667957743621"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Urnov and Kassim propose regulatory frameworks to help disseminate personalized CRISPR treatments to rare disease patients who need them. Without better regulations, every guide RNA nucleotide change necessitates a long (~4 year) process to obtain approval. Many rare diseases can progress quickly, so this time period is often deadly for patients. A fresh approach to trialling treatments for rare genetic diseases could make their production an economically viable prospect at last.", "display_url": "lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/p…", "end": 93, "expanded_url": "https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/personalized-crispr-therapies-could-soon-reach-thousands-heres-how", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113187672005222400/bs0mh9JY?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1066}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113187672005222400/bs0mh9JY?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 70, "status": 200, "title": "Personalized CRISPR therapies could soon reach thousands — here’s how – Lifeboat News: The Blog", "unwound_url": "https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/personalized-crispr-therapies-could-soon-reach-thousands-heres-how", "url": "https://t.co/9bjDg04oTS"}]}, "id": "2113187667957743621", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 116, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Personalized CRISPR therapies could soon reach thousands — here’s how https://t.co/9bjDg04oTS", "url": "https://x.com/LifeboatHQ/status/2113187667957743621"}, {"author_id": "393073854", "created_at": "2026-10-22T10:26:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113215469813415952"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 103, "id": "35789155", "start": 94, "username": "fwpharma"}], "urls